    {
      "id": "8ph6q76",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: INTRODUCTION TO RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) serves as the central bank, regulating the country's monetary system and credit supply.",
        "Primary functions of RBI include issuing currency, acting as the Banker to the Government, and serving as the Banker's Bank.",
        "RBI exercises credit control using quantitative tools such as Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR), Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR), Repo Rate, Reverse Repo Rate, and Open Market Operations (OMO).",
        "Monetary policy tools directly influence inflation, market liquidity, and broader economic development."
      ],
      "id": "8nil26u"
    },
